ential clinically significant medication issues were identified for the patient since their admission?","type":"choice","repeats":false,"readOnly":false,"answerOption":[{"valueCoding":{"system":"http://loinc.org","code":"LA32-8","display":"No"}},{"valueCoding":{"system":"http://loinc.org","code":"LA33-6","display":"Yes"}},{"valueCoding":{"system":"http://loinc.org","code":"LA27681-8","display":"NA-There were no potential clinically significant medication issues identified since SOC/ROC or patient is not taking any medications"}}]},null,{"linkId":"Section-10/J1900A","prefix":"J1900A","text":"The patient exhibits no injury - there is no evidence of any injury noted on the physical assessment performed by the nurse or primary care clinician; the patient has made no complaints of pain or injury; moreover, there has been no change in the patient's behavior after the fall.","type":"choice","repeats":false,"readOnly":false,"answerOption":[{"valueCoding":{"system":"http://loinc.org","code":"LA137-2","display":"None"}},{"valueCoding":{"system":"http://loinc.org","code":"LA6306-0","display":"One"}},{"valueCoding":{"system":"http://loinc.org","code":"LA11073-6","display":"Two or more"}}]},{"linkId":"Section-10/J1900B","prefix":"J1900B","text":"The form asks whether the patient has any minor injuries, including skin tears, abrasions, lacerations, superficial bruises, hematomas, and sprains, or any fall-related injury that has caused them to complain of pain.","type":"choice","repeats":false,"readOnly":false,"answerOption":[{"valueCoding":{"system":"http://loinc.org","code":"LA137-2","display":"None"}},{"valueCoding":{"system":"http://loinc.org","code":"LA6306-0","display":"One"}},{"valueCoding":{"system":"http://loinc.org","code":"LA11073-6","display":"Two or more"}}]},{"linkId":"Section-10/J1900C","prefix":"J1900C","text":"Has the patient had any major injuries such as bone fractures, joint dislocations, closed head injuries with altered consciousness, or subdural hematoma?","